{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftK7zNf6PhDrttat9TZh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Prioritise fixing bank-connection failures at the three large banks, not streaks.**\n\n**Why:**\n- **The best lever in your data is connecting a bank account.** Users who connect in week one retain at 3x the rate of those who don't. Only 34% connect, and 22% of attempts fail.\n- **Failed attempts are users you are losing for no reason.** Someone who starts a connection has already shown intent, and a failure at a bank you don't control is not a motivation problem. If none of those users retry successfully, fixing the failures could lift week-one connection from 34% to about 44%.\n- **Streaks target the wrong behaviour.** People typically check a budget weekly or around payday, so daily use isn't the natural rhythm. A 12% DAU/MAU may be fine. Pushing daily opens tends to raise activity and notification opt-outs, not long-term retention.\n\n**Caveat:** The 3x figure is a correlation, since motivated users both connect and stay. A better test: compare 90-day retention for users whose connection failed against users who succeeded. Both groups showed intent, so if the failed group retains much worse, the fix is likely to pay off.\n\n**Six-week plan (two engineers):**\n1. **Week 1:** Break failures down by bank, error type and data provider. Check how many affected users retry and succeed, and run the failed-vs-succeeded retention comparison.\n2. **Weeks 2–5:** Fix the three banks. Options include a backup data provider, OAuth or authentication fixes, automatic retries and clearer error messages. Add a manual-entry or CSV import option for users who still can't connect.\n3. **Week 6:** Add a few targeted notifications, such as \"your connection failed, try again\" or a weekly spending summary. Avoid daily streak prompts.\n\n**Measure:** Week-one connection rate (main metric), with 90-day retention by signup cohort as the result that matters. Keep a holdout group where you can. If the 66% who never try to connect turn out to be the bigger group, test onboarding changes next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3609,"cache_read_input_tokens":4609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3609},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86cb32a1-5442-45f4-8c7d-d3cd641688bb","uuid":"c0818963-a70d-4781-8da0-a94681d39d0d","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:23:34.284Z","request_id":"req_011CftK7z9WuYLb381XuWrBb"}
